./xmodel/grok-nfd-review.md:50:  **11-A’s table row is the wrong comparison even as a citation.** It writes “`v_2(2Π)=1` vs resonance-side `≥3`” and D4 checks `1<3` as a hardcoded boolean. That is the promoted `H8_EQUAL_QUOTIENT_VP_MISMATCH` certificate (`sol-normalform.md:522-599`), independently replayed here (`P_1=2C` with `C` odd ⇒ `v_2=1`; resonance `P'=4·(2l)/l=8`, later odd multipliers keep `v_2=3`; a `w=3` prefix `A` gives `v_2(8AB)≥3`). It is a mixed charged/neutral comparison. The document’s own remarks put the `5/8` step in NF-P, “same carve as 11-A’s `5/8`.” It is not a computation of the *pure-neutral* window. The pure-neutral 11-A comparison at `μ=1` would have been `1` vs `≥2` (right packet `P_0=4`); at `μ=2` it matches, as above.
