./xmodel/sol-g5-emission.log:2090:./SHEET6.md:8:- **Obtained (free, in `refs/`)**: Orevkov 1986 3-sheet paper (`jc86.pdf`, author-hosted English), Domrina–Orevkov 1998 4-sheet I (`do.pdf`), and — the decisive find — **Sigray's full 66-page 2008 ELTE PhD thesis "Jacobian trees and their applications"** (`sigray_full.pdf`, teo.elte.hu/minosites/ertekezes2008/sigray_i.pdf; booklet `sigray_i.pdf`), advisor A. Némethi.
./xmodel/sol-g5-emission.log:2091:./SHEET6.md:10:- **1c. RECON correction**: "no independent reproof of ≤5 exists" is WRONG. Sigray's thesis Theorem 9.1 proves td(f,g) ≥ 6 for any counterexample, independently of Żołądek, same year, different machinery (decorated Eggers–Wall trees vs Newton–Puiseux charts). Never journal-published (zbMATH lists only his monodromy + kp′q−lpq′ papers) but cited as the bound by Makar-Limanov (arXiv:2106.06869) and Borisov (arXiv:1901.04073: "current best lower bound ... is 6"). Caveats on BOTH proofs: Żołądek's neighboring gcd sections have a **documented gap** (GGV arXiv:1401.1784: Lemma 4.10 "claims without proof that I₂ ⊂ (1/m)Γ(f₂)"; his claimed B>33 fails, B≥16 stands only via GGV's independent reproof) — his topdeg-5 sections have no reported gap but are unaudited; Sigray's thesis is unrefereed. Also flagged: arXiv:2407.13795 (Moskowicz, 2024, 8pp) claims NO Keller map has prime field-extension degree — unpublished, treat as unvetted; if ever verified it would exclude 7 and make 6, 8, 9 the whole frontier.
./xmodel/sol-g5-emission.log:2097:./SHEET6.md:31:- **Verification standard**: exact arithmetic only (PARI/SymPy; no floats, no Gröbner needed at this layer). Every "no solution" needs a certificate: explicit congruence obstruction (with modulus), or monotone bound + finite sweep below it. Two independent implementations per case (repo's dual-build culture); spot-formalize the Diophantine kills in Lean post-verdict. Symbolic residue computations are NOT needed for the Sigray engine (they belong to Żołądek's chart engine, which we'd hold in reserve as cross-check).
./xmodel/sol-g5-emission.log:2098:./SHEET6.md:35:1. **Foundations audit** (blocking): Sigray §§3–8 (Abhyankar-based; unrefereed thesis) and/or Żołądek §§1–3. Given the GGV-documented gap in Żołądek's §4–5, neither source can be trusted un-audited. Human+agent close reading, est. 1–2 weeks. This is the load-bearing risk.
./xmodel/sol-g5-emission.log:2100:./SHEET6.md:40:- **Verdict: realistic weeks-scale multi-agent campaign — NOT a conceptual wall at 6.** The wall (consistent local datum) is proven only at td = 9/(48,64). Prerequisites in order: (a) foundations audit of Sigray §§2–8 [+ fetch Żołądek PDF for the reserve engine]; (b) mechanize + validate on td ≤ 5; (c) sweep td = 6. Even the failure mode (a surviving tree) produces a concrete bidegree target for the existing (72,108)-style exclusion pipeline. Prize: bound becomes td ≥ 7 — with 8-and-9 then the endgame of the whole at-infinity program (and 9 known unreachable locally ⇒ global methods required there regardless).
