./xmodel/sol-g5-emission.log:7782:xmodel/sol-reduction.out-18702-268:with $\kb$ an integer greater than $2$ (integrality by L6 and St.~3.8, corrected). Thus $d_p\mid d_q$ iff $(\kb-2)\mid 2$ iff $\kb\in\{3,4\}$. Finally, at $\mu=1$ we have $d=\nu+1$ and $D\equiv-\ell\pmod{\nu+1}$, so $d\mid D$ iff $(\nu+1)\mid\ell$: the on-axis zero-chain law is the $\mu=1$ specialization.
