./xmodel/sol-prob.log:8553:10:- **1c. RECON correction**: "no independent reproof of ≤5 exists" is WRONG. Sigray's thesis Theorem 9.1 proves td(f,g) ≥ 6 for any counterexample, independently of Żołądek, same year, different machinery (decorated Eggers–Wall trees vs Newton–Puiseux charts). Never journal-published (zbMATH lists only his monodromy + kp′q−lpq′ papers) but cited as the bound by Makar-Limanov (arXiv:2106.06869) and Borisov (arXiv:1901.04073: "current best lower bound ... is 6"). Caveats on BOTH proofs: Żołądek's neighboring gcd sections have a **documented gap** (GGV arXiv:1401.1784: Lemma 4.10 "claims without proof that I₂ ⊂ (1/m)Γ(f₂)"; his claimed B>33 fails, B≥16 stands only via GGV's independent reproof) — his topdeg-5 sections have no reported gap but are unaudited; Sigray's thesis is unrefereed. Also flagged: arXiv:2407.13795 (Moskowicz, 2024, 8pp) claims NO Keller map has prime field-extension degree — unpublished, treat as unvetted; if ever verified it would exclude 7 and make 6, 8, 9 the whole frontier.
./xmodel/sol-prob.log:8557:14:- **(A) Żołądek's Newton–Puiseux charts** (reconstructed from zbMATH + Nguyen Van Chau arXiv:0804.3172v2 + MIMUW seminar abstract): resolve (f,g) at infinity in BOTH source and target; near each divisor use multivalued charts (x^{−1/m}, ξ) — truncated fractional-power series x(Σc_k x^{−k/m} + ξx^{−n/m}) where ξ replaces the Puiseux tail ("left and right Newton-Puiseux charts", Chau). The Keller map becomes near-monomial in charts; jac≡1 forces rigid exponent+leading-coefficient relations. Topological degree = sheets over infinity = Σ local degrees over dicritical divisors, with Orevkov's identity Σ(ramification excess at infinity) = td − 1. Case analysis = finite enumeration of dicritical/chart configurations for td ≤ 5; each killed by exponent arithmetic or analytic contradiction.
./xmodel/sol-prob.log:8562:19:- **Orevkov/Domrina (3,4) were quasi-topological**: splice/Eisenbud–Neumann diagrams of the resolution boundary, homology, intersection form, canonical class K̃ = F*K + B of the branched cover; leaf kills by unimodularity/negative-definiteness/Abhyankar–Moh determinant arithmetic. Case tree at 4: ~19 configurations → 8 final diagrams (Domrina 2000), a few dozen leaves.
./xmodel/sol-prob.log:8563:20:- **The 4→5 explosion is NOT case count — it is a provable method failure.** Egorov 2002 constructed a proper 5-sheeted "exotic covering" of C² (branching along two planes F₁*,F₂*; H²_c ≅ Z²; S₁² = −3, S₂² = −15, S₁·S₂ = −3; K(S₁)=K(S₂)=1) consistent with EVERY quasi-topological invariant Domrina–Orevkov use. So 5 required a new analytic layer: both 2008 proofs inject Abhyankar approximate-root/Puiseux-coefficient arithmetic (pole orders of g along f-branches; jac=1 exponent identities) that sees strictly more than the topology. That is the conceptual jump; the case tree itself only grew ~2×.
./xmodel/sol-prob.log:8574:31:- **Verification standard**: exact arithmetic only (PARI/SymPy; no floats, no Gröbner needed at this layer). Every "no solution" needs a certificate: explicit congruence obstruction (with modulus), or monotone bound + finite sweep below it. Two independent implementations per case (repo's dual-build culture); spot-formalize the Diophantine kills in Lean post-verdict. Symbolic residue computations are NOT needed for the Sigray engine (they belong to Żołądek's chart engine, which we'd hold in reserve as cross-check).
./xmodel/sol-prob.log:8578:35:1. **Foundations audit** (blocking): Sigray §§3–8 (Abhyankar-based; unrefereed thesis) and/or Żołądek §§1–3. Given the GGV-documented gap in Żołądek's §4–5, neither source can be trusted un-audited. Human+agent close reading, est. 1–2 weeks. This is the load-bearing risk.
./xmodel/sol-prob.log:8583:40:- **Verdict: realistic weeks-scale multi-agent campaign — NOT a conceptual wall at 6.** The wall (consistent local datum) is proven only at td = 9/(48,64). Prerequisites in order: (a) foundations audit of Sigray §§2–8 [+ fetch Żołądek PDF for the reserve engine]; (b) mechanize + validate on td ≤ 5; (c) sweep td = 6. Even the failure mode (a surviving tree) produces a concrete bidegree target for the existing (72,108)-style exclusion pipeline. Prize: bound becomes td ≥ 7 — with 8-and-9 then the endgame of the whole at-infinity program (and 9 known unreachable locally ⇒ global methods required there regardless).
