./xmodel/ideation-20260830T1015Z-fable5.log:4:The load-bearing finding is the q=6 attack (packet item 5). I derived the marked-fibre lattice geometry for both surviving rows by hand and found exactly why the q=8 proof does not transfer: at q=6 the strict different is forced to meet both sections once (`C⁽⁰⁾·S = C⁽⁰⁾·T = 1`, versus 0 at q=8), so the disjointness-from-H step and `b_j = 2a_j` both fail; and the `B3/A2` marked fibre necessarily contains a second strict component `M` that breaks the q=8 horizontality lemma and is exactly where the unpromoted `τ=0` modulus cell threatens a vertical different. The correction is `b_j = 2a_j + σ_j`, and the lattice then collapses the extra Euler slack on its own: every q=6 carrier contains both `O`-pair indices where the strict multiplicity is 1, so at most one contracted carrier with coefficient one survives, and affine roots are confined to `I₆` pairs. A desk-scale scratch enumeration (~15 s, standard library, elimination-safe direction only) found **zero pairwise-disjoint survivors in every singleton allocation cell of both rows** — baselines, all 20 one-carrier cells, all μ=1 and μ=2 roots including the borderline ones, the `B3` Δ=0 special cells even with the shared-site pair exempted, and every alternative section-attachment assignment. The open remainder is multi-root/carrier combinations plus a new `B3` special-modulus local table; that is card 1, and if it closes (conditional on the q=8 review), the entire reduced finite fixed-quadratic stratum is empty and all pressure moves to the presentation/selector arrows.
