./xmodel/sol-monodromy.log:1087:SHEET6.md:10:- **1c. RECON correction**: "no independent reproof of ≤5 exists" is WRONG. Sigray's thesis Theorem 9.1 proves td(f,g) ≥ 6 for any counterexample, independently of Żołądek, same year, different machinery (decorated Eggers–Wall trees vs Newton–Puiseux charts). Never journal-published (zbMATH lists only his monodromy + kp′q−lpq′ papers) but cited as the bound by Makar-Limanov (arXiv:2106.06869) and Borisov (arXiv:1901.04073: "current best lower bound ... is 6"). Caveats on BOTH proofs: Żołądek's neighboring gcd sections have a **documented gap** (GGV arXiv:1401.1784: Lemma 4.10 "claims without proof that I₂ ⊂ (1/m)Γ(f₂)"; his claimed B>33 fails, B≥16 stands only via GGV's independent reproof) — his topdeg-5 sections have no reported gap but are unaudited; Sigray's thesis is unrefereed. Also flagged: arXiv:2407.13795 (Moskowicz, 2024, 8pp) claims NO Keller map has prime field-extension degree — unpublished, treat as unvetted; if ever verified it would exclude 7 and make 6, 8, 9 the whole frontier.
./xmodel/sol-monodromy.log:1273:**(a)** Build the log surface of the resolved \(f\)-pencil (vertical boundary + sections). Apply Miyaoka–Yau / Bogomolov–Miyaoka–Yau in orbifold form, or \(\bar\kappa\) constraints, or unimodularity of the splice diagram (Orevkov/Domrina), and obtain a numerical contradiction for a counterexample.
./xmodel/sol-monodromy.log:1275:**(b) Tried on the pinned skeleton.** `SHEET6-CLASSICAL.md` T3: full \((K+D)^2\le 3 e_{\mathrm{orb}}\) **needs B- and x-internal resolution data the template does not pin**. Euler/delta/genus ledger **passes identically**. Integrality witnesses exist (including rational-fiber candidates). Orevkov 3-sheet and Domrina–Orevkov 4-sheet papers are in `refs/` and were the reason td=5 needed a new analytic layer (Egorov).
