./xmodel/sol-monodromy.log:1838:SHEET6.md:20:- **The 4→5 explosion is NOT case count — it is a provable method failure.** Egorov 2002 constructed a proper 5-sheeted "exotic covering" of C² (branching along two planes F₁*,F₂*; H²_c ≅ Z²; S₁² = −3, S₂² = −15, S₁·S₂ = −3; K(S₁)=K(S₂)=1) consistent with EVERY quasi-topological invariant Domrina–Orevkov use. So 5 required a new analytic layer: both 2008 proofs inject Abhyankar approximate-root/Puiseux-coefficient arithmetic (pole orders of g along f-branches; jac=1 exponent identities) that sees strictly more than the topology. That is the conceptual jump; the case tree itself only grew ~2×.
./xmodel/sol-monodromy.log:1843:SHEET6.md:40:- **Verdict: realistic weeks-scale multi-agent campaign — NOT a conceptual wall at 6.** The wall (consistent local datum) is proven only at td = 9/(48,64). Prerequisites in order: (a) foundations audit of Sigray §§2–8 [+ fetch Żołądek PDF for the reserve engine]; (b) mechanize + validate on td ≤ 5; (c) sweep td = 6. Even the failure mode (a surviving tree) produces a concrete bidegree target for the existing (72,108)-style exclusion pipeline. Prize: bound becomes td ≥ 7 — with 8-and-9 then the endgame of the whole at-infinity program (and 9 known unreachable locally ⇒ global methods required there regardless).
