./xmodel/sol-connections.log:3869:SHEET6.md:8:- **Obtained (free, in `refs/`)**: Orevkov 1986 3-sheet paper (`jc86.pdf`, author-hosted English), Domrina–Orevkov 1998 4-sheet I (`do.pdf`), and — the decisive find — **Sigray's full 66-page 2008 ELTE PhD thesis "Jacobian trees and their applications"** (`sigray_full.pdf`, teo.elte.hu/minosites/ertekezes2008/sigray_i.pdf; booklet `sigray_i.pdf`), advisor A. Némethi.
./xmodel/sol-connections.log:3870:SHEET6.md:10:- **1c. RECON correction**: "no independent reproof of ≤5 exists" is WRONG. Sigray's thesis Theorem 9.1 proves td(f,g) ≥ 6 for any counterexample, independently of Żołądek, same year, different machinery (decorated Eggers–Wall trees vs Newton–Puiseux charts). Never journal-published (zbMATH lists only his monodromy + kp′q−lpq′ papers) but cited as the bound by Makar-Limanov (arXiv:2106.06869) and Borisov (arXiv:1901.04073: "current best lower bound ... is 6"). Caveats on BOTH proofs: Żołądek's neighboring gcd sections have a **documented gap** (GGV arXiv:1401.1784: Lemma 4.10 "claims without proof that I₂ ⊂ (1/m)Γ(f₂)"; his claimed B>33 fails, B≥16 stands only via GGV's independent reproof) — his topdeg-5 sections have no reported gap but are unaudited; Sigray's thesis is unrefereed. Also flagged: arXiv:2407.13795 (Moskowicz, 2024, 8pp) claims NO Keller map has prime field-extension degree — unpublished, treat as unvetted; if ever verified it would exclude 7 and make 6, 8, 9 the whole frontier.
./xmodel/sol-connections.log:3871:SHEET6.md:14:- **(A) Żołądek's Newton–Puiseux charts** (reconstructed from zbMATH + Nguyen Van Chau arXiv:0804.3172v2 + MIMUW seminar abstract): resolve (f,g) at infinity in BOTH source and target; near each divisor use multivalued charts (x^{−1/m}, ξ) — truncated fractional-power series x(Σc_k x^{−k/m} + ξx^{−n/m}) where ξ replaces the Puiseux tail ("left and right Newton-Puiseux charts", Chau). The Keller map becomes near-monomial in charts; jac≡1 forces rigid exponent+leading-coefficient relations. Topological degree = sheets over infinity = Σ local degrees over dicritical divisors, with Orevkov's identity Σ(ramification excess at infinity) = td − 1. Case analysis = finite enumeration of dicritical/chart configurations for td ≤ 5; each killed by exponent arithmetic or analytic contradiction.
./xmodel/sol-connections.log:3873:SHEET6.md:19:- **Orevkov/Domrina (3,4) were quasi-topological**: splice/Eisenbud–Neumann diagrams of the resolution boundary, homology, intersection form, canonical class K̃ = F*K + B of the branched cover; leaf kills by unimodularity/negative-definiteness/Abhyankar–Moh determinant arithmetic. Case tree at 4: ~19 configurations → 8 final diagrams (Domrina 2000), a few dozen leaves.
./xmodel/sol-connections.log:3876:SHEET6.md:40:- **Verdict: realistic weeks-scale multi-agent campaign — NOT a conceptual wall at 6.** The wall (consistent local datum) is proven only at td = 9/(48,64). Prerequisites in order: (a) foundations audit of Sigray §§2–8 [+ fetch Żołądek PDF for the reserve engine]; (b) mechanize + validate on td ≤ 5; (c) sweep td = 6. Even the failure mode (a surviving tree) produces a concrete bidegree target for the existing (72,108)-style exclusion pipeline. Prize: bound becomes td ≥ 7 — with 8-and-9 then the endgame of the whole at-infinity program (and 9 known unreachable locally ⇒ global methods required there regardless).
