./xmodel/sol-wtc1r2.log:13431:./xmodel/grok-reduction-review.md:99:- How checked. Żołądek Theorem 6.12 gives \(td\ge 6\). GGV22's “\(\max(\deg P,\deg Q)\ge 125\) or \((72,108)\) or transpose” is a *lower*-bound dichotomy in *polynomial* degree, and only for the GGV-minimal lane. GGV5 Algorithm 8 is complete only under an input bound \(v_{1,1}(A_0)\le M\). `SHEET6-TDUNIFORM.md` §7: no finite residual list uniform in \(d\); composite single-pole searches grow \(4\to 212\) from \(d=6\) to \(d=16\). Moskowicz arXiv:2407.13795 (no prime field-extension degree) is unpublished and unused, correctly. No sheet theorem, no GGV theorem, and no Sigray theorem supplies \(td\le N\).
