./xmodel/sol-wtc1r2.log:13524:./xmodel/codex-eval-20260812.md:3046:SHEET6.md:10:- **1c. RECON correction**: "no independent reproof of ≤5 exists" is WRONG. Sigray's thesis Theorem 9.1 proves td(f,g) ≥ 6 for any counterexample, independently of Żołądek, same year, different machinery (decorated Eggers–Wall trees vs Newton–Puiseux charts). Never journal-published (zbMATH lists only his monodromy + kp′q−lpq′ papers) but cited as the bound by Makar-Limanov (arXiv:2106.06869) and Borisov (arXiv:1901.04073: "current best lower bound ... is 6"). Caveats on BOTH proofs: Żołądek's neighboring gcd sections have a **documented gap** (GGV arXiv:1401.1784: Lemma 4.10 "claims without proof that I₂ ⊂ (1/m)Γ(f₂)"; his claimed B>33 fails, B≥16 stands only via GGV's independent reproof) — his topdeg-5 sections have no reported gap but are unaudited; Sigray's thesis is unrefereed. Also flagged: arXiv:2407.13795 (Moskowicz, 2024, 8pp) claims NO Keller map has prime field-extension degree — unpublished, treat as unvetted; if ever verified it would exclude 7 and make 6, 8, 9 the whole frontier.
