   112	
   113	## 3. Hostile attacks by cluster
   114	
   115	### 3.1 Hamiltonian \(\kappa\) and weight slices
   116	
   117	The attractive part is exact, but it also exposes the restatement risk.  If
   118	\(P_x,P_y\) generate the unit ideal, choose
   119	\(V=A\partial_x+B\partial_y\) with \(V(P)=1\), and put
   120	
   121	\[
   122	  D_P=P_y\partial_x-P_x\partial_y,
   123	  \qquad \kappa(P)=[\operatorname{div}V]
   124	  \in \mathbb C[x,y]/D_P\mathbb C[x,y].
   125	\]
   126	
   127	Any two such \(V\)'s differ by \(hD_P\), and
   128	\(\operatorname{div}(hD_P)=D_P(h)\), so the class is well defined.  Moreover,
   129	\(\kappa(P)=0\) lets one subtract \(hD_P\) to make \(V\) divergence-free.
   130	Polynomial de Rham exactness in two variables then writes
   131	\(V=Q_y\partial_x-Q_x\partial_y\), giving \([P,Q]=1\).  The converse is
   132	immediate.  Thus
   133	
   134	\[
   135	  \boxed{\kappa(P)=0\iff P\text{ has a polynomial Keller mate}.}
   136	\]
   137	
   138	That is a useful exact coordinate on the gap, but a universal theorem that
   139	every atypical end pairs nontrivially with \(\kappa(P)\) is essentially the
   140	missing theorem unless the pairing is independently computable on a proper
   141	class.  The quotient is also close to classical Brieskorn/Petrov-module and
   142	relative de Rham constructions, creating a serious **PRIORITY** risk.
   143	
   144	The weight version is cheaper and can be honest if it freezes a proper
   145	no-leak class.  One proposed deformation is invalid before weights enter:
   146	
   147	\[
   148	  P=x+x^2y+y^k.
   149	\]
   150	
   151	For every \(k\ge2\), \(P_x=1+2xy=0\) gives \(y=-1/(2x)\), and
   152	\(P_y=x^2+ky^{k-1}=0\) becomes a nonzero equation
   153	\(x^{k+1}=-k(-1)^{k-1}/2^{k-1}\), which always has a complex solution.
   154	Hence this proposed “hostile deformation” is never unimodular.  The \(k=1\)
   155	case also has common critical points.
   156	
   157	**Adversarial disposition:** **REDESIGN, then launch one bounded gate.**  First
   158	do a priority/equivalence freeze for \(\kappa\).  Then prove a complete weight
   159	recurrence only for a certified unimodular family such as
   160	\(P=x+x^ny\), with an explicit no-leak lemma.  Accept
   161	`VALID-FAMILY-NO-GO`, `LEAK`, or `KNOWN-MODULE`; do not accept a universal
   162	“residue should see every end” heuristic as progress.
   163	
   164	### 3.2 Dual-pencil vanishing divisor
   165	
   166	For a hypothetical Keller pair, every target-linear member
   167	\(H_{[a:b]}=aP+bQ\) has no affine critical point.  The proposed next object,
   168	however, is not yet a divisor.  An infinity-defect function in a one-parameter
   169	pencil can have a positive generic value.  In that event its support is all
   170	of \(\mathbb P^{1\vee}\), not a finite effective Cartier divisor.  Subtracting
   171	the generic value may produce a jump divisor, but loses the claimed direct
   172	positivity and changes the degree formula.
   173	
   174	This is not a technicality: for a counterexample there is no prior reason
   175	that a generic linear projection has zero infinity defect.  Establishing
   176	generic vanishing is already very close to obtaining a coordinate member of
   177	the pencil.  Likewise, `J=1` trivializes an affine two-form but does not by
   178	itself force a degree-zero effective boundary divisor under GRR.  Any such
   179	step must exhibit the missing determinant line and its sign, or it is the
   180	same **COSTUME/RESTATEMENT** failure as the earlier raw boundary passports.

