23-MSC:                                                We study 2-dimensional Jacobian maps using so-called Newton–Puiseux charts. These are
24-primary 14R15                                       multi-valued coordinates near divisors of resolutions of indeterminacies at infinity of the
25-secondary 14E07                                     Jacobian map in the source space as well as in the target space. The map expressed in these
26-                                                    charts takes a very simple form, which allows us to detect a series of new analytical and
27-Keywords:                                           topological properties. We prove that the Jacobian Conjecture holds true for maps (f , g)
28:Polynomial map                                      whose topological degree is ≤5, for maps with gcd(deg f , deg g) ≤ 16 and for maps with.
29-Jacobian Conjecture                                 gcd(deg f , deg g) equal to 2 times a prime.
