136-    Using the Newton–Puiseux expansions (in the source space) and the quasi-Puiseux expansions (in the target space) we
137-can easily calculate the ramification indices of dicritical divisors of resolution. Moreover, it is possible to obtain a subtler
138-characterization of the divisors of resolution; we shall divide them into four types: Abhyankar, non-properness, transitory
139-and infinite.
140:    The effectiveness of our method is demonstrated in a direct proof of the Orevkov–Domrina theorem and its generalization
141-to 5-sheeted maps. As another application we present an elementary proof of the Jacobian Conjecture in the cases
142-gcd(deg f , deg g) equals 2 times a prime (improvement of the Appelgate–Onishi theorem) and gcd(deg f , deg g) ≤ 16
143-(improvement of Heitmann’s result).
144-    We hope that the present paper will form a solid basis in the search for a counter-example to this conjecture. (After
145-failing to get a contradiction in the analysis of Jacobian maps, the author began to be more and more convinced about the
--
148-survey articles by Bass, Connell and Wright [4], by Drużkowski [9], by van den Essen [12], by the author [34] and to the
149-recent book of van den Essen [13].
150-    The plan of the paper is the following. In Section 2 we define Newton–Puiseux charts and use them in the resolution of
151-indeterminacies at infinity of one polynomial. In Section 3 we resolve the indeterminacies of a non-invertible Jacobian map;
152-there we introduce the quasi-Puiseux expansion and give a classification of the Newton–Puiseux charts (Theorem 3.14).
153:Sections 2 and 3 form a basis of our study of the Jacobian maps. So, at the end of Section 3 we outline the results proved
154-in the further sections. Here we only give localization of the main theorems: the generalizations of the Appelgate–Onishi
155-and Heitmann theorems (Theorems 4.7, 4.12 and 4.16) are given in Section 4 and in Section 6 we generalize the
156:Domrina–Orevkov’s result (Theorem 6.12). In the Appendix we prove some lemmas about Schwarz–Christoffel integrals
157-and we provide a list of the main notations.
