1853:In this section we prove that B = 16 or B > 20, and that B 6= 2p for all prime p. The first result
1854-can be inferred from [7, Theorem 2.24], whose proof is hidden behind a computer search. We give
1855-a complete proof, without the use of a computer. Abhyankar allegedly developed a proof of the
1856-second result according to [7, Page 50], but we could not find any published article of Abhyankar
1857-with such proof. Heitmann says that it is possible to adapt the proof of [7, Proposition 2.21]
1858-to prove B 6= 2p, however we were not able to do this. On the other hand this is also claimed
1859:to be proven in [15, Theorem 4.12]. But the proof relies on [15, Lemma 4.10], which has a gap,
