    39	  \operatorname{td}(F)=[\mathbb C(x,y):\mathbb C(P,Q)],
    40	\]
    41	
    42	not total polynomial degree.  Domrina's 2000 four-sheet theorem excludes a
    43	four-sheeted polynomial map \(\mathbb C^2\to\mathbb C^2\) with nonzero constant
    44	Jacobian (Izvestiya: Mathematics 64:1; MathNet `im273`).  The repository's
    45	`ladder/SHEET6.md` records the independent ladder: three sheets by Orevkov,
    46	four by Domrina, and \(\operatorname{td}\leq5\) closed by the later
    47	at-infinity work.
    48	
    49	Consequences:
    50	
    51	- `MAPPING-DEGREE-FOUR`, `QUARTIC-RESOLVENT-OPEN-CHART`, and
    52	  `N4-FILLING-NIELSEN` are **PRIORITY-ERROR / KNOWN-CASE**, not research roots.
    53	- The honest next sheet frontier is \(\operatorname{td}=6\).  It is already an
    54	  active, sharply funnelled campaign in `ladder/SHEET6-CAMPAIGN.md`: four
    55	  single-pole `r9/M2` carriers and the unique merged two-pole child remain.
    56	  Any sheet-topology capacity should continue those named gaps (not reopen
    57	  held cells and not reconstruct rank four).
    58	- Even without Domrina, the three proposed quartic mechanisms were not ready.
    59	  A finite quartic algebra need not be globally monogenic; a cubic resolvent
    60	  is not thereby a polynomial Keller map with source \(\mathbb A^2\); and an
    61	  \(S_4\)-valued inertia presentation does not bound the braid or branch-curve
    62	  geometry.  Thus none supplied an exhaustive quartic reduction.
    63	
    64	This correction removes an entire apparent consensus cluster.
    65	
    66	### 1.2 The advertised “first HC4 quintic module” already ran and failed
    34	## 2. Canonical corrections before ranking
    35	
    36	Four post-collection checks materially alter the raw vote.
    37	
    38	### 2.1 Mapping degree four is already closed
    39	
    40	The packet highlighted Orevkov's exclusion of multiplicities two and three
    41	but omitted the campaign's already banked continuation.  Domrina's 2000
    42	general-case theorem excludes four-sheeted complex plane polynomial maps
    43	with nonzero constant Jacobian, and Żołądek Theorem 6.12 proves invertibility
    44	for topological degree at most five.  The canonical sheet ledger in
    45	`ladder/SHEET6.md` and `ladder/SHEET6-CAMPAIGN.md` already says `td <= 5`
    46	closed.
    47	
    48	Therefore `MAPPING-DEGREE-FOUR`, `QUARTIC-RESOLVENT-OPEN-CHART`, and
    49	`N4-FILLING-NIELSEN` are `PRIORITY-ERROR/KNOWN-CASE`.  They are not launched
    50	and may not be retargeted by replacing `4` with `6`.  The honest first sheet
    51	frontier remains `td=6`, already funnelled into the existing sheet-six and
    52	residue-A/global-landing program.
   146	## 7. Attack routes (if ABSENT / SOURCED-PARTIAL)
   147	
   148	1. **Chart-Jacobian / N–P route (Żołądek 6.7 + Chau chart).** In a resolved non-properness chart, `μ_l = l−k` and `Jac θ̃ = v^{l−k−1}`. Show that a Keller map cannot have a dicritical chart with `l−k=1` (i.e. `θ̃` étale along `v=0` while `P∘θ̃` stays finite-valued and nonconstant). Chau’s `det DF_φ = −m J t^{n−2m−1}` is the unresolved-chart analogue; the missing lemma is the transformation of that order under the remaining blowups that produce a smooth map-dicritical. Desk-scale, one valuation.
   149	
   150	2. **Image-singularity / covering route (R8+R13+R4, repairing Chain D).** Make the series-to-line identification a numbered lemma (Chau 2011 covering + Φ-chart from Chau 2004 Lemma 1 proof). Then split `μ=1` by `s_l`: `s_l=1` plus immersive image plus Jung `d>e>1` is the AMS obstruction; `s_l≥2` is a polynomial parametrization of degree `≥2` whose reduced image is singular, and the collapsed map is an unramified cover of `C^2 \ A_F` along that component — a π1 computation on the complement of a singular uniruled curve (Jelonek), not a simply-connected slogan.
   151	
   152	3. **Unique-versus-mixed split at general `N`.** R12 almost kills unique `μ=1` at `N=4`; rewrite that step with corrections visible (R3), then decide the mixed remainder `(μ=2)+(μ=1)` which is the SHEET-GATE transposition-class bit and the BUDGET-N `m_triv` coefficient. Borisov’s ample ramification divisor (R19) is a possible global obstruction to a numerically trivial summand, but only after checking that an unramified type-3 curve is still in the support.
   153	
   154	## 8. Acquisition list for a successor proof lane
   155	
   156	Pin as PDFs, with hashes, before any promotion:
   157	
   158	1. Official Math. USSR-Izv. typesetting of Orevkov 1987 (IOP / Math-Net), to confirm Lemma numbers against `refs/jc86.pdf`.
   159	2. Lê Dũng Tráng–C. Weber, Kodai Math. J. **17** (1994), 374–381 (journal PDF).
   160	3. Abhyankar–Luengo, Amer. J. Math. **133** (2011), 1713–1732.
   161	4. Abhyankar, Indian J. Pure Appl. Math. **41** (2010), 77–97.
   162	5. Journal form of Chau 2004, Ann. Polon. Math. **84** (2004), 203–210 (vs arXiv:math/0305088v1).
   163	6. Gwoździewicz, Rocky Mountain J. Math. **32** (2002), 99–126 (or the published version of the Euclid record).
   164	7. Cassou-Noguès–Daigle, Adv. Stud. Pure Math. **75** (2017), 7–28 (full text).
   165	8. Domrina, *Four-sheeted polynomial mappings of C^2. The general case*, Izv. Math. **64** (2000), 1–33 (two-dicritical companion of R12).
   166	9. Fourrier, Ann. Inst. Fourier **46** (1996), 645–687 (topology at infinity; cited by Cossart).
   167	10. The “principal lemma of [4]” backing Cassou Remarque 4.8 (identify and pin that reference).
   168	
   169	Not needed to start a proof lane, but useful: Neumann–Norbury classification of simple rational polynomials; Campbell, *Partial properness and the Jacobian conjecture*.
   170	
   171	<!-- BODY-END -->
